# {{ artifact_label }}

Drafts one {{ artifact_label | lower }} for one {{ entity_singular }}. Quality
depends entirely on the matching — picking the right 1-2 proof points from
`proof_bank.md` for *this specific {{ entity_singular }}* — not on generic
prose-polishing. Genericness is the failure mode to actively fight.

{% if has_coaching %}
## Work authorization stays out of drafts

Never mention visa status, work authorization or sponsorship in a draft unless
they ask you to. Whether and when to raise it is their call.

{% endif %}
## Inputs

- **The {{ source_label }}**: a URL to fetch, or text pasted directly by
  the caller. Read the whole thing — not just a bullet list, what the
  other side actually seems to care about.
- **Profile/background doc** — required. Look for
  `{{ config_dir_name }}/profile.md` first; if it's not there, check the
  folder for *any* PDF/doc file before concluding there isn't one — people
  often drop in a resume or bio under its own name (e.g.
  `jane-doe-resume.pdf`) rather than renaming it to `profile.md`. Only stop
  and ask for one if the folder is genuinely empty of anything usable.
- `{{ config_dir_name }}/proof_bank.md` — the primary source of specific,
  tailored proof points. If this file only has the EXAMPLE entry (or
  doesn't exist yet), fall back to `profile.md` directly, and say plainly
  in your output that the draft is lower-tailoring quality because the
  proof bank isn't filled in yet — don't silently produce a generic draft
  without flagging why.
- `{{ config_dir_name }}/voice.md`, if present — sample past writing.
  Match its tone, sentence rhythm, and level of formality. If absent, use
  the default voice below.
- Optionally, a `{{ entity_singular }}_id` from the tracker (when called by
  {{ entity_singular }}-scout-agent, or when you reference a specific
  queued/{{ baseline_stage | lower }} row directly) — if given, write the
  result into that row's `{{ artifact_field_prefix }}_draft` column instead
  of just returning text.

## Default voice (used only when voice.md is absent)

Direct, confident, first-person, plain sentences. No throat-clearing. Say
the specific thing, not the category of thing.

**Banned phrases** — a starting list, adjust to your domain. Never use
these or close variants in default voice unless a real voice sample shows
you actually write this way:
- "I am writing to express my interest in..."
- "I believe I would be a great fit because..."
- "I've always been passionate about..."
- "team player" / "hard worker" / "go-getter" / "self-starter"
- "I look forward to hearing from you" as a sole closing line with
  nothing else

## Process

1. **Read the {{ source_label }} closely.** Pull out 2-4 things that
   actually matter here — not just a copy of the requirements/description,
   but what seems to actually be the crux of it.

2. **Match against the proof bank.** For each of the 2-4 things
   identified, find the entry whose tags/content most directly proves it.
   Pick the best **1-2 entries total** for the whole draft — resist the
   urge to cram in three or four; going deep on one or two real, specific
   proof points beats skimming five. If nothing in the proof bank is a
   good match for what actually matters most here, say so in your output
   rather than forcing a weak match.

3. **Draft**, roughly 250-350 words (3-4 short paragraphs) unless voice
   samples suggest a different length works better:
   - **Opening** (1-2 sentences): specific to this {{ entity_singular }} —
     name the actual thing that connects to the proof point you're about
     to bring in. Never open with generic enthusiasm and nothing concrete
     backing it up.
   - **Body** (1-2 paragraphs): one matched proof point per paragraph,
     using its "punch version" if the entry has one (adapt lightly to fit
     this {{ entity_singular }}'s specific language rather than pasting
     verbatim), explicitly tying the result back to what's actually being
     asked for.
   - **Close** (1-2 sentences): confident, specific next step.
   - Never invent achievements, numbers, or experience not present in
     `profile.md` or `proof_bank.md`. If the fit is genuinely thin, write
     a shorter, honest draft rather than padding with invented specifics.

4. **Deliver.** A draft isn't done until it's a real file — you'll want to
   upload these to forms/sites directly, not hand-copy text out of a
   database column.
   - Write the draft to `{{ config_dir_name }}/{{ artifact_dir_name }}/{id}_{primary}_{secondary
     slug}.txt` (slug = alphanumerics only, hyphen-joined; primary/secondary
     taken from the tracker row, or from context if called standalone).
     Create the directory if it doesn't exist. Write it with the file-writing
     tool, not a shell heredoc.
   - If called with a `{{ entity_singular }}_id`: write this SQL with the
     file-writing tool to `{{ config_dir_name }}/{{ artifact_dir_name }}/.update.sql`
     (overwrite it each time), then run exactly
     `psql -d {{ db_name }} -f {{ config_dir_name }}/{{ artifact_dir_name }}/.update.sql`.
     A file plus one plain `psql -d` command needs no quoting tricks and is
     what the unattended daily run is allowed to do.
     ```sql
     UPDATE {{ entity_plural }}
     SET {{ artifact_field_prefix }}_draft = $draft$...$draft$,
         {{ artifact_field_prefix }}_file_path = '/absolute/path/to/the/.txt/file'
     WHERE id = <id>;
     ```
     Store the *resolved absolute path* — the dashboard's "Reveal file"
     button needs a real path, not a relative one. Confirm briefly,
     including the file path.
   - If called standalone (no id — a one-off {{ entity_singular }} you
     mention in chat, not something in the tracker): still write the file
     (pick a sensible name under `{{ config_dir_name }}/{{ artifact_dir_name }}/`
     without an id prefix), tell the path, and give a one-line note on
     which proof-bank entry/entries you used and why, so the matching
     logic can be sanity-checked, not just the prose.

{% if scout_outreach_mode %}
## Direct outreach mode

Used when {{ entity_singular }}-scout-agent flags a {{ entity_singular }} as
inviting direct contact (the posting names a person or an email address, or
says to skip the form) instead of a standard blind application. The caller
passes the contact (name and/or email, if known) along with the source text.

This produces a short **email**, not a formal {{ artifact_label | lower }}, so
it differs from the default process above:

- **Shorter**: 100-180 words, not 250-350. One matched proof point, not two —
  this is a first note, not a full pitch.
- **Opens with a real greeting** addressed to the contact by name if known
  (`Hi {Name},`). If only an email address was found, open with a line that
  refers to the specific thing they posted, never a generic "To whom it may
  concern."
- **Closes lower-friction**: something like "happy to send more detail or jump
  on a call this week" — this is a cold note to a person, not a document
  attached to a form, so the ask should read like the start of a conversation.
- Same rules otherwise: no invented achievements or numbers, no banned
  phrases, and pick the one proof point from `proof_bank.md` the same way.

**Delivery differs too**: write the file with an `_outreach` suffix
(`..._outreach.txt`) so you can tell at a glance it is an email body for a
specific address, not a document to upload. Still write it into
`{{ artifact_field_prefix }}_draft` / `{{ artifact_field_prefix }}_file_path`
when called with a `{{ entity_singular }}_id`. If a contact email was found,
say so plainly in your confirmation (e.g. "note also names foo@company.com as
the contact") — that is the whole point of this mode, and it has to reach the
person reading this, not just sit in a notes column.

{% endif %}
## Notes for {{ entity_singular }}-scout-agent callers

When invoked as part of a queueing run, keep the per-candidate cost down:
don't re-fetch the {{ source_label }} if the caller already has the text in
hand — pass it through instead of re-fetching. Skip invocation entirely for
candidates where `{{ artifact_field_prefix }}_needed` is clearly `false`.
